domain StructuredSemanticAuthoringKernelDesignV1Acceptance:
  description "Record exact owner acceptance of D11 implementation-design revision two without authorizing implementation."
problem P1:
  |
    Determine the lifecycle state and authority boundary after the owner replied
    ACCEPT to the independently re-reviewed D11 design revision two.
evidence E_DESIGN:
  |
    The reviewed design is Seal
    c4f8cb366d788d49a5769a7ec3cf2e31d97704a0c9eff17a4e23862330319394.
    It is implementation-design candidate v1 revision two for PERT task cb215.
evidence E_REVIEW:
  |
    Review Seal d7144b116dec2b708cd8252ae4aea1d1078f3248123e86cd0c87734045aeee89
    reports PASS with no P0, P1, P2 or P3 findings and recommends ACCEPT of
    the exact design Seal.
evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-11, immediately after the re-review result was presented, the
    product owner replied ACCEPT.
premise ACCEPTED_POINTS:
  |
    The accepted design includes its proposed policy defaults of eight provider
    calls and 500000 micro-USD per attempt, additive projection of owner-answer
    need onto the legacy failed status, recovery through a new source-reconstructed
    attempt, and the specified no-progress and cycle thresholds.
premise BOUNDARY:
  |
    Acceptance establishes the exact D11 implementation design and completes its
    design gate only. It does not authorize implementation, provider calls,
    evaluation, deployment, production migration, candidate acceptance, pointer
    or policy activation, rollback, release or successor-task start.
premise DOWNSTREAM_OBLIGATIONS:
  |
    Exact DTO and focused-patch elaboration, durable process-loss takeover, the
    fifteen-case one-to-one mapping, public owner-Q&A route mapping and runtime
    evidence remain required at the downstream gates identified by the review.
decision ACCEPTANCE based_on P1, E_DESIGN, E_REVIEW, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE, ACCEPTED_POINTS, BOUNDARY, DOWNSTREAM_OBLIGATIONS:
  |
    Record exact D11 implementation-design revision two as Accepted. Complete
    PERT task cb215 while leaving cb206 and every later implementation or runtime
    task unstarted and separately authorized.
